MView Day 25 (2026-10-06)
=========================

Microscopy edition, step M0: the plug-in points in the core (user)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
"ok go with m0. a new dev/specs document in its own subfolder is needed"
The microscopy edition is a second program from the same source tree
(Day 24). M0 prepares the shared core for it, so that the edition's
units can plug themselves in and MView never notices: in MView every
new list is empty and every name is what it was in 1.0.1.

- uEdition (new): EditionId ('MView'), EditionTitle ('Versarite
  MView'), EditionVersion (MViewVersion = '1.0.1'); SetEdition, called
  first in an edition's .lpr; EditionIniFileName = <exe folder>\
  <EditionId>.ini.
  Used by: uConfig (the settings file; the CONFIG_FILE constant is
  gone), uSingleInstance (mutex 'Local\Versarite<EditionId>.Instance',
  mapping 'Local\Versarite<EditionId>.Window': for MView the same names
  as before), uIniEditor (captions), uMainForm (About box and its menu
  entry, captions, the welcome picture <EditionId>_welcome.png). The
  About box keeps the dedication.
- uExtensions (new), three registries, filled by the edition's units in
  their initialization sections:
  - metadata readers: TImageMetadata (reader, pixel size in um, lines
    for a panel); ReadImageMetadata asks them in order, the first that
    understands the file wins, one that gives up or raises leaves
    nothing behind. Pure functions, any thread. No caller yet (M2).
  - overlay layers (TOverlayLayer: Picture, Version, HandleMouse; the
    registry owns them): drawn by both renderers over the image, lens
    and selection, under the info line, badge, notice and panels. The
    GPU keeps a texture per layer, uploaded again when Version or the
    size changes. Mouse: after the badge, filter panel and magnifier,
    before the sort panel and the mouse language; not over the open
    sort panel; the layer that takes a press gets its release wherever
    it is; a move or leave a layer takes still reaches the sort panel
    (its edge). A layer's exception costs its picture or its mouse
    event, never the paint or the mouse language. OverlayChanged ->
    TMView repaints.
  - menu entries (caption, action, enabled / checked tests): the main
    form adds them before "About" as a group of their own; Enabled and
    Checked asked each time the menu opens.
- Test: TestExtensions.lpr / .lpi (needs BGRABitmap, so built by
  lazbuild like TestGif); build_test.bat builds and runs it.
- Review (independent, as no compiler is at hand here): no compile
  errors found. Fixed from it: a layer's press now captures its release
  (else a release over the sort panel was lost, or a layer could
  swallow the panel's release after a swipe); a leave a layer takes
  still reaches the panel; GPU re-uploads a layer's picture on a new
  size; Picture wrapped in try/except in both renderers; MenuEntry
  range check; the dedication comment back above HandleAboutMenuClick;
  the menu item list cleared when the viewer ends.

