How to switch between the editions (user asked)
-----------------------------------------------
Not an ini switch: the edition decides which ini is read, and MView must
not carry the microscopy code. Each edition is its own project: open
MView.lpi or MViewLab.lpi in Lazarus and build; both exes can sit in
build\ and run at the same time.

M1: the skeleton program, Versarite MView Lab
---------------------------------------------
Name and repository as proposed (Versarite MView Lab, id MViewLab; same
repository), the user not objecting.
- MViewLab.lpr: MView.lpr plus SetEdition('MViewLab', 'Versarite MView
  Lab', '0.1.0') first thing, and uEdition, uExtensions and the
  edition's units in the uses list.
- MViewLab.lpi: MView.lpi (with the user's Debug / Release modes) with
  target build\MViewLab, source\microscopy on the search path, its own
  unit folder build\units-lab\.
- MViewLab.ico: MView's lens and torii with a teal "fluorescence" sky,
  to tell the two apart on the taskbar.
- source\microscopy\uPixelProbe.pas, the first edition unit: menu entry
  "Show pixel position" (checked while on): a small label next to the
  mouse with the image pixel under it. Watches the mouse, never takes
  it; draws its label only when the text changes. It exercises every
  plug-in point the measuring line and scale bar will use.
- Core change found on the way: TOverlayLayer.Picture now also returns
  the picture's place (out ALeft, ATop) and the picture is only as
  large as what it shows; a whole-view picture would mean a 4K texture
  upload on every mouse move. Both renderers and TestExtensions updated
  (a quarter-view box in the middle: size and place checked).
- Review (independent): no compile errors found; three nits taken (the
  image size falls back to the bitmap's when the full size is unknown;
  a needless FillTransparent; an unused unit).
Spec: specs\microscopy\..._v0.1 updated (status, switching, what the
two programs share in one folder, the Picture contract, Sec. 4.5 the
pixel probe, roadmap M1 built, decision 9).

To build: open MViewLab.lpi in Lazarus, build. Reload uExtensions,
uRenderer, uGLRenderer in MView too (the Picture change), and rerun
build_test.bat (TestExtensions changed).

- MViewLab.ico, first build: "bitmap with unknown compression". The
  icon had PNG entries at every size; Lazarus reads the small ones as
  BMP. Now one 256 px PNG entry, like MView.ico.
- The fixed icon was written back over by Lazarus: it keeps the
  project's icon in memory and writes it to MViewLab.ico when it saves
  the project. Fixed from inside Lazarus (Project Options, Application,
  Load Icon: MViewLab_256.ico). Rule from now on: .ico / .lpi / .res of
  a project open in Lazarus are changed only with the project closed.
- MViewLab builds and runs (user).

