M2a: the .lif reader
--------------------
- source\microscopy\uLifFile.pas (no LCL): header, UTF-16 XML (fcl-xml
  DOM), block index; images with path, size, z / t, pixel size
  (Length / (N - 1), as readlif; the check against a burned-in bar stays
  open), z step, channels and LUT colours, objective, zoom, pinhole,
  scan, active detectors, time taken; one channel's plane; all channels
  in colour, one plane or the maximum projection.
- A Python reference reader (container only) gave the expected values
  for sample.lif: 24 images; e.g. Image003 1024 px 0.28409 um/px;
  Series009 12 z-planes (its z Length is 0 in the file: no step).
- test\TestLif.lpr (plain fpc, in build_test.bat): a small .lif made by
  the test, damaged files, and sample.lif when it is there (it stays
  private).
- Review (independent): no compile errors; all expected values
  recomputed and right. Taken: the XML goes to the parser as raw UTF-8
  bytes (outside the LCL a string could be converted to the ANSI code
  page and a name with a non-ASCII letter would not parse); a cut-off
  block's size is clamped to what is in the file.

