M2b: containers like folders
----------------------------
Planned with an independent read of the core (folder listing ->
navigator -> key -> loader -> info line), then built:
- source\utility\uContainers.pas (new, no LCL): readers' registry;
  virtual names 'C:\data\sample.lif|Series009' ('|' can't be in a
  Windows path: always virtual, and missed code fails safe); helpers
  ItemDirectory, ItemExists, RealFolderOf, DisplayItemName
  ('sample.lif › Series009'), ItemBaseName ('sample_Series009').
- Hooks, all no-ops without a reader (MView): uDirectoryTree (a
  container listed with the folders, its entries its images; a
  container root), uDirectoryImages.Scan, uDirectoryScanner.Resolve and
  its rebuild, uNavigator (ItemDirectory; OpenPath), MakeImageKey (the
  container's size and time), uMediaLoader (virtual names decoded by
  the reader, memory guard, I/O gate), uMView (info line, sorting
  refused for an entry, FolderOnDisk, saved names, TC follow and its
  cursor on a .lif), uMainForm (TC side by side and the sort menu:
  FolderOnDisk), uRenderer (error text), uImageSaver (names).
- source\microscopy\uLifContainer.pas (new): registers .lif; unique,
  safe ids; stacks as their maximum projection.
- MViewLab.lpr: uContainers, uLifFile, uLifContainer.
- TestNavigation: TestContainers (a fake '.fak' reader, one entry per
  line): nothing changes before it is registered; after it, the tree,
  the listing, next / previous folder into and out of the container,
  opening the container, an entry, resuming on an entry, ListedKey.
- Review (independent): one compile error (an edit had put a function
  body into the interface of uContainers), fixed; MView without a
  reader traced unchanged on every path. Taken: the up gesture inside a
  container works as in any folder (no special case: the old one would
  have jumped back to the folder's first image); a real folder named
  *.lif is not a container (FileExists checks); the memory guard before
  the bitmap; unique ids for images of the same name; TC's cursor on a
  .lif; the error text shows the entry's name.
- Open: containers in non-recursive opens (M2c side panel); a cached
  index per .lif (each listing and decode parses its description).

