M2c: containers in the side panel
---------------------------------
Planned with an independent read of uSortPanel / uSortFolders / TMView;
built in two parts:
- Model and listing: TDirectoryImages keeps the folder's container files
  apart (AddContainer, ContainerCount, Container; a container's own
  listing: its neighbours); the tree fills them; TNavigator.
  FolderContainers. TPinnedContainers ([Containers] Pinned1..N) in
  uSortFolders, owned by TConfig, written only when an edition reads
  containers (never into MView.ini).
- The panel: the container group below "+", a grey folder with a star
  (amber .lif, cyan stack, violet other) where the numbers used to be
  (the dead DrawBadge became DrawStar); pinned ones have "..." = unpin.
  Contents mode: "< back", then the images with thumbnails; hover = the
  large one in the box left of the panel; click = show it in the view.
  Double-click a container = its images; swipe / wheel click = open it
  in the view. A .lif dropped on the panel is pinned.
- uContainerThumbs (new, source\imaging): the list and the thumbnails on
  a thread of their own (the hovered one first, the I/O gate, the newest
  request replaces the older).
- Tests: TestNavigation (container lists of folders, of a container,
  the tree, Assign, FolderContainers; none without a reader), TestSort
  (TPinnedContainers round trip, removed keys go).
- Review (independent): no compile errors; MView unchanged. Fixed from
  it: the thumbnail thread redid its work every second (the wait's
  timeout); the container list could stay empty when the background tree
  filled it in later (the list is now part of the refresh key); the
  footer's own notes were hidden in contents mode; a delivery that
  raises doesn't lose the rest; back only with the left button.

