Esc to the settings: at once, the viewer closes in the background (user)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
"when leaving the window with esc, the loading time for the ini window is
several seconds" - the viewer's destructor waited for its threads (a
decode under way is finished, not interrupted: the 12-19 MB TIFFs; the
scanner; the .lif thumbnails up to 1 s; a copy; a save) before the
settings appeared. User: "put everything into the background ... the
save ini button has to be buffered, maybe with a little moving timer
icon".
- TJobScheduler.BeginShutdown / WorkersStopped, TDirectoryScanner.
  BeginShutdown, TFileMover.DropWaiting / Working, TContainerThumbs.
  BeginShutdown / Stopped: stop without waiting, ask later.
- TMView.BeginClose (settings saved once - the destructor doesn't again -,
  everything told to stop, no more deliveries) / CloseFinished (polled;
  the read gate released once the workers are back).
- TMainForm.ReturnToEditor: BeginClose, the settings at once, the viewer
  kept as FClosingViewer; FCloseTimer (50 ms) frees it when finished
  (at most 15 s, except a copy under way); a new viewer, Exit, the form's
  end finish it first.
- TIniEditor.Busy: a turning ring at the right of the button bar; Save
  (Ctrl+S) and View images (F5) kept and done when the viewer is gone.
- Review (independent): no compile errors. Taken: the exit deadline
  knows a copy in the closing viewer (no cut-off copy); the kept save is
  done before the viewer is freed (a stuck read can't lose it); a
  finished scanner is waited for, not abandoned (it leaked); the window
  place stored again after a kept save; text changed after a kept save
  makes Exit ask again.
- Tried (user): "the window shows instantly, but it is an empty frame and
  it takes several seconds to fill". The real cost: FPC's TIniFile
  rewrites the whole file on EVERY Write unless CacheUpdates is on;
  TConfig.Save writes ~60 keys = ~60 rewrites of MView.ini (each also
  looked at by the virus scanner), and Esc did it twice (the viewer's
  settings, then the settings screen completing the file). Now every
  TConfig writer (Save, SaveSort, SaveFilters, the save folder,
  SaveWindowBounds) and uImageScale's choice: CacheUpdates, one
  UpdateFile at the end.
- Tried (user): "it feels like it got worse ... settings should be written
  when changes occur, except for the last file/last directory".
  TConfig.Save now works in memory (TMemIniFile: one read) and writes the
  file only if its text differs (usually just LastFile / LastDirectory).
  And the Esc path is timed: ms after the key for each step (window,
  views, viewer saved+stopping, menus, ini read / completed, editor
  shown, ini text, mouse page, settings screen, drawn = first idle tick,
  threads back, viewer freed) in the settings' help line - to see where
  the seconds really go.
- Measured (user's screenshot): window 176, views 224, viewer saved +
  stopping 224, ini read / completed 224, editor shown 5856, ini text
  5856, mouse page 10640, settings screen 10912, drawn 10960, threads
  back 10960, viewer freed 10992. Neither the threads nor the ini: the
  "Mouse & keys" page - every button / key row has 3 drop-down boxes of
  ~70 commands; showing the screen pushed them all into Windows (5.6 s,
  the form's window is made again when leaving fullscreen), loading the
  profile filled them all again (4.8 s).
- uMousePage: a box holds only its chosen entry (FLazy = its index in
  the full list) until it is opened or entered (OnDropDown / OnEnter:
  EnsureFilled); ShowRow / WriteRow work with ComboIndex. The timing
  line stays until the user has checked it.
- Measured again (user): window 160, ini completed 208, editor shown
  1392, mouse page 1520, settings screen 1856, drawn 1904. "better, but
  still a delay". The rest: leaving fullscreen set BorderStyle, and LCL
  makes the form's window again for that - every control of the hidden
  settings screen (and AcceptDropsOn's HandleNeeded on each) is made
  anew. Windows: the frame (WS_CAPTION, WS_THICKFRAME) switched with
  SetWindowLongPtr + SetWindowPos(FRAMECHANGED), no new window; other
  systems keep BorderStyle.
- Measured again (user): window 64 (the frame fix works), editor shown
  1104 (from 144), settings screen 1488. Started in the viewer (Mode=1),
  so the first Esc builds the settings screen: the "Mouse & keys" page's
  ~80 controls, a layout per control. Now: the page's rows are made when
  its tab is first shown (TMouseProfilePage.BuildRows / PageShown), and
  ShowEditor lays the screen out once (DisableAutoSizing).
