Formats (user; discussion recorded, for the implementation plan)
----------------------------------------------------------------
The user's comparison (specs\Versarite_MView_Viewer_Comparison.docx):
formats are MView's weak point. Xelitan's Pascal libraries looked at
(XelImageFormats, AVIF/HEIC pure Pascal LGPL-2.1, JPEG XL via libjxl,
JPEG 2000, WebP): a reference, not a dependency (young, licences).
Decided (user): modern formats (HEIC, AVIF, WebP, JPEG XL) through
Windows' own codecs (WIC) in MView and Image Lab; no large licence
overhead ("this is a fun project"); microscope makers' files one at a
time as containers (Leica first, then .czi / .nd2 / .oir / .vsi when
files come); the TIFF options and the symbiosis with Fiji (ImageJ / OME
scale, 16-bit, stacks). Spec "Microscopy edition" Sec. 9b, decision 14.
Next: the user tests the calibration; then M3b step 3 (settings tab).

